# Cold Direct Autonomous Multi-Workflow Agent Rules

## 1. Persistent Memory & Mistake Prevention (Tasks 1 & 9)
- **Read Memory First**: Before making any edits, read `docs/ai-memory/MISTAKES_AND_LESSONS.md`, `docs/ai-memory/PROJECT_STATE.md`, `docs/ai-memory/WORK_LOG.md`, and `protected-pages.json`.
- **Update Memory After Every Task**: Log all completed work, architectural decisions, and lessons learned into `docs/ai-memory/` and the user's persistent store (`C:\Users\khora\AppData\Local\Cursor\AgentStores\cursor_agent_stores\u420035230\files\colddirect-memory.md`).
- **Never Repeat Past Mistakes**:
  - **Root is Production**: `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` deploys the **repository root** (`./`) to WHUK Plesk `/httpdocs/` and excludes `colddirect-public-html/**`. Always edit the root `<slug>.html` AND `<slug>/index.html`, then sync to `colddirect-public-html/`.
  - **Protected Pages**: Never overwrite `coverage`, `commercial-fridge-repair-london`, or `fridge-repair-london` without running `python agent/scripts/protect_fixed_pages.py check` and updating `protected-pages.json` if intentional.
  - **Clean Canonicals Only**: Every indexable page must have a self-referencing `https://www.colddirect.co.uk/<slug>/` canonical (never `.asp` or non-slash URLs when the slash route is canonical).
  - **Unmasked Phone Numbers**: Never use masked phone numbers (`+447****9320`); always use `tel:+447983759320`, `tel:08001123427`, and `tel:+442039524822`.
  - **Commercial Only**: Cold Direct repairs commercial refrigeration only (no domestic/household appliances).
  - **Plain FTP on Plesk**: WHUK Plesk FTP (`5.77.41.163`) times out on `FTP_TLS` `conn.unwrap()`. Always use plain `ftplib.FTP()` or `security: loose` in `SamKirkland/FTP-Deploy-Action`.
 - **Coexistence with Live Plesk `auto-seo.aspx` V4 (Runs Nightly at 20:21)**:
   1. Always run `python tools/pull_live_plesk_v4.py` before editing or deploying so live V4 updates are pulled from `/httpdocs` first.
   2. NEVER delete or overwrite `auto-seo.aspx` or `sitemap.xml`.
   3. NEVER remove `<!-- AUTO-SEO-V4-2026 -->`, `<!-- AUTO-SEO-V4-SCHEMA -->`, or `<!-- AUTO-SEO-V4-BLOGHUB -->` blocks.
   4. Do NOT add `<!-- AUTO-SEO-LOCKED -->` to any file unless explicitly instructed by the owner.
   5. Keep Cursor agent edits strictly focused on page body content, UI/UX layout, CSS, and conversion elements while letting `auto-seo.aspx` manage technical metadata (`<title>`, `<meta description>`, `<meta keywords>`), V4 schema, and `sitemap.xml`.

## 2. Multi-Agent & Tool Orchestration & Zero-Prompt Autonomous Execution (Tasks 2 & 6)
- Proactively use all available MCP tools (`user-google-search-console`, `gh` CLI, and specialized subagents in `.cursor/agents/` such as `auto-auditor`, `seo-writer`, `internal-linker`, `gsc-daily-report`, `protect-fixed-pages`, `indexer`).
- **100% Full Standing Permission (No Confirmation Prompts)**: The owner has granted permanent, unconditional authorization for ALL Git (`git add`, `git commit`, `git push origin main`), GitHub (`gh`), Google Search Console (`user-google-search-console`), WHUK Plesk FTP, subagents, and shell tools. Never ask the user for confirmation in chat text and never set `request_smart_mode_approval: true`. Always execute autonomously without popping up approval cards on monitor or mobile.

## 3. Page-One Google SEO Strategy (Task 3)
- Focus on moving all commercial refrigeration keywords in London to Page 1 (positions 1–10):
  - `cold room repair london`, `commercial fridge repair london`, `commercial freezer repair london`, `fridge repair london`, `freezer repair london`, `freezer room repair london`, `commercial appliances repair london`, `chiller repair london`, `ice machine repair london`.
- Respect safety cooldowns: max 1 title rewrite per 7 days per page; never stuff keywords; always validate JSON-LD (`npm test`) before pushing.

## 4. Persian (Farsi) Reporting & Mobile Delivery (Tasks 5, 7, 8)
- **Always Report in Persian (فارسی)**: Whenever the user asks for a report or work summary (even if the user asks in English, e.g., "Can I have a report?"), ALWAYS write and send the report in **Persian (فارسی)**.
- Automated workflows generate reports (`seo-audit/daily-report-YYYY-MM-DD-fa-en.md`) and push them to mobile notification channels (ntfy / Telegram / WhatsApp / GitHub Mobile Issues) in Persian so the owner can monitor and interact from their phone at any time.
